  "id": "Compound::DB01197 - Gene::6564",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence from the hetionet dataset strongly suggests a mechanistic link between Captopril and Slc15a1, mediated through Fosinopril. Captopril, an Ace Inhibitor, is causally associated with conditions such as Skull Hypoplasia, Oligohydramnios, and Microsomia, all of which are linked to Fosinopril. Fosinopril, a similar class of drug, binds to Slc15a1, a protein involved in ion transport and cellular homeostasis. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a shared biological mechanism. The low common ancestor of Captopril and Fosinopril as Ace Inhibitors and Organooxygen Compounds further supports a common pharmacological pathway. The integrated evidence suggests that Captopril’s effects on Slc15a1 are likely mediated through Fosinopril, highlighting a potential role in disrupting ion transport processes, which could contribute to the developmental and physiological effects observed in the associated conditions. The mechanistic link is robust, but the exact cellular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
